Your task is to convert natural language into a knowledge graph, updating an existing graph structure.

You will be given all previously stored data in the Memgraph graph database, designated by <data>. The data is in the form of a CYPHERL file. Note the entities and relationships which already exist in the graph, and their types.

Next, you will be given a prompt in natural language, designated by <prompt>.
The prompt comes from a file, given after <file_path>.
The file is stored in a repository, given after <repo_path>.

Identify the entities, relationships and attributes which should be added to the already existing graph. Pay attention to the types of the new entities, relationships and attributes.

CRITICAL CYPHER CONSTRAINTS:
- NEVER generate standalone MATCH statements (they are invalid and will cause database errors)
- Use only CREATE, MERGE, and SET statements to update the knowledge graph
- To reference existing nodes, use MERGE with ON CREATE and ON MATCH clauses
- Every statement must create, merge, or update nodes and relationships
- Every NODE MUST have at least one LABEL. Choose from the taxonomy:
	Person, Organization, Company, Technology, Publication, Initiative, Facility, Application, Award.
	If none apply, use the fallback label Unknown (i.e., :Unknown).
- Do NOT create unlabeled nodes (labels(n) must never be empty)
- Always set 'file_path' and 'repo_path' attributes on all nodes and edges
- End each statement with a semicolon

VALID UPDATE CYPHER EXAMPLES:
```cypher
MERGE (p:Person {{name: 'John Doe'}})
ON CREATE SET p.file_path = '/path/to/file.md', p.repo_path = '/repo/path'
ON MATCH SET p.updated = true;

MERGE (c:Company {{name: 'Tech Corp'}})
ON CREATE SET c.file_path = '/path/to/file.md', c.repo_path = '/repo/path';

MERGE (p)-[:WORKS_FOR {{file_path: '/path/to/file.md', repo_path: '/repo/path'}}]->(c);
```

INVALID CYPHER (DO NOT GENERATE):
```cypher
MATCH (p:Person {{name: 'John Doe'}});                    // INVALID - standalone MATCH
MATCH (c:Company) WHERE c.name = 'Tech Corp';           // INVALID - standalone MATCH
MATCH (p:Person)-[:WORKS_FOR]->(c:Company);             // INVALID - standalone MATCH
CREATE (n {name: 'No Label'});                          // INVALID - unlabeled node
```

Convert the prompt into valid Cypher CREATE, MERGE, and SET statements only.
Pay special attention to relationship directions and ensure all entities have proper attributes.
Set the attribute 'file_path' of every new node and edge equal to the source of the prompt.
Set the attribute 'repo_path' of every node and edge created equal to the repository where the prompt comes from.